On 29 Oct 1998, root wrote:

> I've seen hints of glibc 2.1, but can't find
> it anywhere. I'm running 2.07 now, but would
> like to upgrade...

 Glibc 2.0.9x are the current glibc 2.1 alpha (i.e. pre-beta and not
Alpha) releases. But beware, upgrading to 2.0.9x breaks some programs
which need to be recompiled. Some programs do not work properly after
recompilation.  You may need the current snapshot of egcs if you wish to
compile the library yourself.

 Upgrade only if you desperately need some of its features or you enjoy to
experiment.

