In article <3637732C.5EA9DE05@spam.sirius.com>, Kevin Miller wrote:
>Like everyone else who has been posting here, I am interested in the
>cheep price of the Multia.  I have been looking for something small, and
>reasonable fast to use in a somewhat embedded application to play mp3s
>in my car.  Can anyone tell me if the Multia 166 machines can decode an
>mp3 stream at full bitrate with any degradation or skipping.  Note that
>this would be all the system would be doing.  Thanks

Yep, a UDB 166 uses about 60% CPU running mpg123 decoding a 112kbit
MP3 bitstream.

I'm not sure I'd recommend one for this application, though:
 - The drive probably won't much like being vibrated
 - The system runs quite warm, and you will need to provide sufficient
   ventilation.  My UDB cooked itself to death just sitting on my desk.

A StrongARM might be better suited for this, but they're not quite as
cheap as a UDB.  OTOH you might be able to get a bare-bones board with
just the StrongARM, memory, and IDE controller for cheaper.  I don't
know where, though.

-andy



