hgm@saunalahti.fi wrote:
: I got problems with few applications.
: Many of them will compile without errors ,but they don't run!
: This is output which I logged when I runned xquake :
: -
: X Error of failed request:  BadAccess (attempt to access private 
: resource denied)
:  Major opcode of failed request:  129 (MIT-SHM)
:  Minor opcode of failed request:  3 (X_ShmPutImage)
:  Serial number of failed request:  37
:  Current serial number in output stream:  38
:  VID: shared memory id=513, addr=0x15555556000
:  VID: shared memory id=514, addr=0x15555576000
: These errors come out only when running X programs ,please help me !
What version of Linux Kernel are you using?
Older 2.0.* kernels are known to have a IPC bug which disables X shared
memory. For 2.0.30 you can apply the Alpha diffs that can be found on
gatekeeper which will fix this.
If it is not X-SHM then you might have encountered a miss-feature of Alpha
X servers not beeing able to handle X shared pixmaps (whatever that is...).
Some applications rely on this, others handle this by using other methods. A
fix is not yet known.
CU
