Shack - the one that is supposed to Y off a "large" connector into one "large"
and one "small" (floppy) connector, then connected the floppy connector to
the Multia connector and the other side of the Y to the drive (with the 
connector that was originally supposed to connect the Y to the main power
dangling in the middle). This gives me a connector that is about 18" long
total - long enough to reach outside the Multia box, where my disk drive is
mounted. Seems to work great!

Hope this helps!

