>> With kernels 2.1.115 and below the sound worked just fine. and since there
>> doesn't seem to have been some sound changes in 115-116 it must be something different.
>
>I compiled my first 2.1.x kernel (126) today and noticed the same problem.
>Remembering seeing this post I checked out using the sound driver sources
>from 115 (didn't check if they differed), which compiled fine but produced
>the same fault.

On the AlphaStation 200, of the type that came from ONSALE in large quantities
recently, I had the same problem. Sound died between 2.1.115 and 2.1.116. I 
went crazy trying to figure it out.

It is NOT the sound drivers themselves at fault. It is the PCI code. Should 
you indeed have the same box, or any 'avanti' based system, the code just 
needs a little patch. The following fix worked for me:

--- linux/arch/alpha/kernel/sys_sio.c.orig      Sat Oct 24 15:24:56 1998
+++ linux/arch/alpha/kernel/sys_sio.c   Sat Oct 24 12:06:46 1998
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@
 avanti_pci_fixup(void)
 {
        layout_all_busses(DEFAULT_IO_BASE, APECS_AND_LCA_DEFAULT_MEM_BASE);
-       sio_pci_fixup(noname_map_irq, 0x0b0a090f);
+       sio_pci_fixup(noname_map_irq, 0x0b0a0e0f);
        sio_fixup_irq_levels(sio_collect_irq_levels());
         enable_ide(0x26e);
 }

