Jo <jofr@iname.com> wrote:
: Hi!
Hello!

: How big are the diffrences between a Alpha-Board SX and LX with 533MHz?
Speed ;)
In short: the LX is significantly faster than the SX but also significantly
more expensive.
The LX use the 21164A CPU whuch has a 1MB internal 2nd level cache and
external 3rd level cache whereas the SX has no 2nd level cache but only
externel 3rd level cache.
The SX uses the 21164PC CPU which is the low cost version.
The LX has some other advantages too but I do not remember right now. All in
all I would estimate that the LX is about 30% faster than the SX but nearly
twice as expensive.
Bothe the LX and SX are discontinued right now!

: Greetings Jo
