Hi,
 
I noticed, that several owners of a ruffian-board have serious problems.
Mine is working very stable and I have no more problems with
syslogd/klogd.
 
What to do :
 
1) Use the newest ldmilo.exe and milo

ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/ldmilo-ruffian-981020

ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/milo-ruffian-981020

2) build your own kernel with

ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/alpha-sources-2.0.35-0.1.tar.gz
  
3) use a special clock-executable
 Sorry, but I have no ftp-space. You can send me an e-mail - I'll send a
uudecoded 
 version.
   
4) don't try to use the internal net-device with 100MBit/s.
 Instead of it, use another PCI-card and configure it as eth1 (e.g. a
21140
 based card).
 I had less problems with 10MBit/s.

 
In this configuration I had no problems with syslogd/klogd. 
 
 
 
Tillmann
 
 
