: causes "Floating exception   Exit 136", while on Intel PII is says:
: "c =    Inf", which is the "correct" answer.

Read gcc documentantion, especially this part which explains
what various -mieee-... options are about and compile using one
of these (liek -mieee, for example).

: Is there any way to make the Alpha do the same thing as PII ?

Yep, but this has a performance impact as exceptions have to
be serialized.

: I know about linking with -mieee, but that makes programs run
: too slow, so that is not a solution for me.

Oh, so you heard some things. :-)  If you do not care about
values on exceptions you can always install "do nothing" signal
handler for SIGFPE (see 'man signal' for details). But how about
'-mieee-with-inexact'?

  Michal




