Andrew D Lenharth wrote:
> 
> I was wondering what I would have to go through to get a multia to boot
> from floppy with the / mounted over nfs.  Can I even get something like
> this to install?

Actually you can even do it without the floppy.  I have an
AS200 that I network boot.  To do it without the floppy you
will have to use the srm console instead of arc and build a
network bootable kernel using aboot.   Read the SRM-HOWTO
for more info here.

As far as mounting / vi nfs you should be able to do that
by configuring the kernel to use nfs for it's root.  On the 2.0.X
kernels this is just after you say "y" to if you want NFS.
Note, you cannot complile nfs as a module for this to work.

Read /usr/src/linux/Documentation/nfsroot.txt
Lots more info there.

- Doug



