I like www.dynastexpress.com for memory.  I just got two lifetime
warranty 32MB ECC SIMMS from them, they turn out to be TI RAM.  Seems
like a good price too.

The Seagate drive should be able to connect to your AS, though if it
has a 68 pin interface, you'll need a 50 pin to 68 pin convertor.
SCSI drives, as far as I have ever known, are backwards compatible, so
even though, by the presence of the W in the model number, that drive
should be capable of 40MB/s througput, you'll probably only be able to
use 10MB/s of that.  Unless of course your AS has an aftermarktet SCSI
controller in it.  

