Hmm ... good question ;)
It should not make much difference if you are using libc5 or glibc as far as
the emulation itself is concerned. All Intel code is passed through the
emulator which uses the Intel libs and the syscalls are passed to the
kernel. Just the em86 binary itself would have to be glibc or libc5.
I do not know if a glibc binary exists, sorry.

