First of all, this is not the correct answer. Dividing by zero is
nonsense. So actually the Alpha is right. What you mean, but what is
completely different, is that when dividing by smaller and smaller
numbers (in the limit /approaching/ zero) the resultant goes to infinity. 

If you don't want to check every divisor and handle exceptions you may 
want to search the documentation to see if you can trap these
exceptions. But that was already suggested by somebody else. 
