I had the same problem and fixed it this way:

If you are in ARC console change to the SRM console.
http://www.mindspring.com/~ccsf-lug/AS200.htm has instructions on making the
firmware disk needed to do this.  You will need two disks, one readable by
the ARC console and the other readable by SRM.

Once you get to the SRM prompt (>>>) type :date yyyymmddhhmm  (enter)
Example 199810221045, type :date (enter) it should now display the new date
and time.
Change back to the ARC console, now your time and date can be set correctly
from ARC

