Create a disk using rawrite with the yourmachine-s.img file from the images
directory.
Create a disk "          "          "       "    ramdisk.img         "
"      "      "           ".
Put the yourmachine-s.img disk in the floppy drive.
at the SRM prompt enter:
boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
prompt_ramdisk=1"
After decompressing the vmlinux.gz, it will ask you to put the ramdisk in the
floppy.
After that it will go into the setup screen for the Redhat installation.

Good luck!

