Norbert Kuemin wrote:
> 
> I've got my AlphaStation 250 on Monday (I've to say im new @ Alpha).
> After some adventures with milo and srm i've mad a redhat 5.1
> installation over ftp.
> 
> I know most of the HW included (TGA, NCR, Tulip) but what kind
> of Soundcard can i use?? I've read something about MSS but if I
> recompile the kernel (2.1.125) mit MSS and the default options
> the sounddriver takes the same irq like the ncr53c810 and everything
> stops.
> 
> Anyone a hint ??


Yep. I've got the same AlphaStation 250 on my desk. Rumours are correct,
the Soundcard is indeed MSS compatible. The default settings are:

(from /etc/conf.modules)
options ad1848 io=0x530 dma=3 irq=9
options opl3 io=0x388

(from menuconfig)
<M> Sound card support
...
<M> OSS sound modules
...
<M> Microsoft Sound System support
...
<M> FM synthesizer (YM3812/OPL-3) support

Small problem however: While the base address can be configured with
jumpers, the IRQ line is hardwired to IRQ9. Unfortunately, INTA of the
second (the lower one) PCI slot is routed to IRQ9, too, so if you have a
PCI-Card installed in this slot, sound cannot be used without hacking
the kernel a bit.

As of kernel 2.1.125, the following pseudo-patch may be used:
file: arch/alpha/kernel/sys_sio.c

static inline void __init
avanti_pci_fixup(void)
{
	layout_all_busses(DEFAULT_IO_BASE, APECS_AND_LCA_DEFAULT_MEM_BASE);
-	sio_pci_fixup(noname_map_irq, 0x0b0a090f);
+	sio_pci_fixup(noname_map_irq, 0x0b0a0e0f);
	sio_fixup_irq_levels(sio_collect_irq_levels());
	enable_ide(0x26e);
}

This reroutes the PCI slot to IRQ14, which appears to be unused in the
AlphaStation 250.

> BTW, ist there a xquake client for Alpha?

Yes, "somewhere out there", though I havent got a pointer handy right
now.

Gruss,
	Matthias



