: problem with 2.1.x kernels on 164sx machines or is it only my machine?
: has anybody been able to boot a 2.1.x kernel on a 164sx?
This is a known problem and you should install a small kernel patch to avoid
this. The patch applies cleanly to all kernels > 2.1.120. You can find the
patch on
  http://www.unix-ag.org/Linux-Alpha/Architectures/SX164.html
along with other useful information.
If you want to use the RTC you may want also to include a patch from Mikolaj
J. Habryn that fixes some user space hangs. The patch is so small so I
attach it here:

--- linux-2.1.124/arch/alpha/kernel/entry.S.orig        Fri Oct  9 17:26:52
1998
+++ linux-2.1.124/arch/alpha/kernel/entry.S     Fri Oct  9 17:32:44 1998
@@ -552,7 +552,6 @@
 ret_from_sys_call:
        cmovne  $26,0,$19               /* $19 = 0 => non-restartable */
        /* check bottom half interrupts */
-       bne     $1,ret_from_handle_bh
        ldq     $3,bh_active
        ldq     $4,bh_mask
        and     $3,$4,$2


: bye,
: Andreas
CU
  nils

