Well... I did 3 linux -> Multia installs last night... all 3 of my
setup floppies were created with rawrite, although they needed to be
formatted (regular ol' FAT) prior to creation.  

Once you get to the MILO> prompt you need to put the BOOT floppy into
the drive and type:

	boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

A bunch of stuff will crusie by on the screen and then it will tell
you to insert (my favorite word) the ROOT floppy (aka the RAMDISK
floppy)..    do so an then hit ENTER  (make sure you have the Red Hat
CD in the drive).

The menu driven installation should begin at this point.  When you get
to the part where you need to partition the disks, I'd suggest you use
FDISK rather than Disk Druid.  It's a bit more complicated, but it
works reliably, whereas Disk Druid does not always do the trick.

You can grab grab the step-by-step instructions from

	http://www.starshipcorp.com/redhat50.html

The 5.0 instructions are the same as 5.1

Good luck !

Ron

