I bought one of their Multias from onsale.com.  Here's what I added:

  - 32 meg TRUE parity RAM (2 4x36) @ ~$56.  I went to www.pricewatch.com
and checked out the True Parity RAM section.  I ended up buying from Dynasty
Express.
  - External SCSI connector.  My multia came with the internal 50pin IDC
SCSI cable permanently connected to the board.  A part from QVS
(www.qvs.com), part number CC691P, extends this to a 50pin microD external
connector @ ~$18
  - I used an external SCSI 1.0 gig hard drive and CDROM that I got from
work.
  - Monitor, keyboard, and mouse I had lying around.

That's it.  All in all, it's working pretty good.

