I have 21164 with the qlogic single ended scsi controller.  This controller offers
very high speed performance, however, being that it is single ended, you CANNOT mix
internal and external devices. It throws off the impedence which causes your
internal drives to become corrupted.  I had to buy a second controller to use the
external devices, scanner, dvd-ram, syquest etc......

You might be able to install the tape drive internally.

Hope this helps.

BTW at least with linux you get the fdsik which corrects the problem, on Windows NT
4.0 running on my Alpha 500a, I had to reinstalled the OS everytime the SCSI
controller corrupted the filesystem.  Windows NT is a piece of shit, but I have to
use it......

