You'd have probably had problems installing Linux from SRM.  I *had*
to get the update and flash it before I could boot (MILO got very
confused - booted with wrong amount of RAM "detected", and locked up
later).  Upgrading tp the latest firmware (and switching to ARC) works
great.

>  Been reading all of the posts and visited a
> bunch of the web sites.  Should I be looking at getting more memory -
> sounds like 32Mb isn't enough from some of the other posts, or is it
> video memory (for X) that is needed?

You need lots of (system) memory for X if you want to run in high-res
high-color modes.  You need a card with a decent amount of video
memory to even *display* said modes. :)

