donas@my-dejanews.com wrote:
> 
> does anybody here know how to change to SRM from AlphaBIOS????
> 

On some machines it is simply a menu selection that says something
like "switch to Digital UNIX console".  However several models only
allow one firmware image; (AlphaBIOS) or SRM to be installed at
once.

If this is the case you need to update your firmware.  The image 
can be found on:

	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v5.2/<model>/<image>.exe

Assuming you have an AlphaStation 200 the exact file is:


ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v5.2/alpha200/as200_v6_8.exe

format a floppy with a DOS filesystem and copy this .exe file to
fwupdate.exe

From the AlphaBIOS menus you should see something about a firmware
update.
Select this (with the floppy inserted) and it should reboot into the
firmware update utility.  From the "update" menu select "SRM".  Power
cycle
and it should come up with the good old ">>>" prompt.

- Doug



