G. Hugh SONG (ghsong@\"Spamspoiler\"kjist.ac.kr) wrote:
: Hi,

: I installed the RedHat 5.1 on a fresh hard.
: Oh, no!   All the links and the directories are dated at year 2018.
: How can I fix this?  The month and day are all right.

My system is a multia, but probably is similar to what you are
running into. If you are booting linux from the ARC firmware, you
need to specify that the clock is in the ARC format. That is where
your 20 year offset is coming from. Another problem that occurs is
that there is a bug in clock (at least with arc/multia) where it
doesn't set the time properly on boot, and i was losing something
like 4 years every boot. By removing a flag from the clock command
in the startup script i fixed that. You probably need a ARC=true in
your /etc/sysconfig/clock file.

As far as fixing the dates on all your directories, you can probably
do a find . -type d -exec touch --time=whatever {} \; 
or similar incantation.


--
