Could you email me the TGA documentation, I would be interested in helping
out with this.  These TGA cards are really nice, it would be a shame to
have to scrape it.

> > 1. In "regular" text mode (i.e., before running X), the cursor
> > appears one space AFTER the actual cursor position (i.e., there
> > appears to be a space between the last character typed and the
> > cursor). This doesn't happen in Xterms, so it's no big deal,
> > but...
> 
> It appears to be an interaction between MILO and the console
> code.  A small change to the terminal driver fixes it for MILO,
> but then the cursor is offset to the left for SRM/aboot
> configurations.  The newer fbcon development kernels don't have
> this problem (namely by not using the hardware cursor), so I
> haven't investigated what was happening.
> 

Actually the problem is in the kernel source code in the file "tga.c".
The problem is in tga_set_cursor on the line where it said 
"col = idx % 80"
it should read 
"col = idx % 80 - 1"

Check out my homepage under Alpha Linux, I have a patch on there:
http://www.cse.buffalo.edu/~pjjarosz

Paul




