connector.  If you need external 68-pin, then Symbios' own
UW controller (I don't know the exact model name.) is the best.
If you need external 50-pin, Diamond's FirePort 40 is the best.
Other no-name controllers using the Symbios UW chip are OK.
But they don't usually have the auto termination.

Gerard Roudier's commitment for the best Linux SCSI driver
made the Symbios controllers the best choice for Linux.
His recent sym53c810.c version 0.8 even works on my Alpha/Linux.

Older ncr53c810.c was known to be faster than Adaptec 2940UW.
Now Roudier said that the new sym53c810 is about 20 %  faster
than ncr53c810.c of course under very heavy load.

--
