In a previous article, Dean Baldwin <dean@intergraphica.co.uk> said:
>I have been trying to use ulimit -n 1024 to set the maximum open files
>to 1024. At the moment
>I get a message saying operation isn't permitted. I get the feeling that
>this needs to be changed
>at a kernel level and recompiled. Does anybody have any thoughts on
>this?

As root, you have to do:

echo "2048" > /proc/sys/kernel/file-max

That sets the maximum allowed for the entire system.

I have no idea if that will allow you to raise the per-process limit on the
number of files.

