"G. Hugh SONG" <ghsong@\"Spamspoiler\"kjist.ac.kr> writes:

> This result implies that the two output "record" files are
> significantly different.
> Even if they both use IEEE-format, there is extra bits of
> information appended on the fortran output files must also
> be different.

Yes, a Cray writes an 8-byte record length expressed in WORDS, not
BYTES.

Linux/Alpha writes an 8-byte record length in bytes.

Linux/x86 writes a 4-byte record length in bytes.

It is fairly trivial to write a conversion program. There is a
record length at the start and end of each record.

-- g



