Well, as far as the graphics cards go, I think the S3 is the only one
that has an X-Server for the Alpha, but if your Alpha has a built-in
one or comes with one, stick with that for awhile.  None of the AGP
cards will work ever, AGP is a special sort of port on Intel machines
especially for graphics cards.  Neither will the Diamond Monster 3DII,
it is ONLY for 3D, so only games that use it's GLIDE API can take
advantage of it.  I'd hold off one the graphics card, it would seem
that there will soon be full support for the Matrox Millenium (the
original one) and that is still one of the finest 2D cards ever.
You're not really going to need a high-powered graphics card either,
your Alpha is not fast enough to take advantage of it.

As for the modem.  Buy an external, leave your internal ports open,
avoid WinModem problems, and have a device that you can connect to ANY
computer.  I have Sun SPARCs with SBUS busses, no way to use an
internal modem there.  It's a lot easier to troubleshoot an external
modem too.  I'd go with a USR external, I've bought quite a few other
modems because they were cheaper, but they just weren't as good.

