Has anybody thought about working on a better TGA driver for X? The 24-plane
patch seems to make the current driver work for the 24-plane TGA boards, but
the current driver admittedly uses no acceleration features of the card. I
poked around a bit in the X-server stuff, and it appears to require more 
expertise than I have. However, I would be interested in helping out where I
could. 

On a different but somewhat related note... My TGA board and X driver has a 
couple of idiosyncrasies I would like to fix, that may be solvable without a 
new X driver. I was wondering if anybody knows what to do about these - they
are minor inconveniences, but it would be nice if they were fixable:

1. In "regular" text mode (i.e., before running X), the cursor appears one space
   AFTER the actual cursor position (i.e., there appears to be a space between
   the last character typed and the cursor). This doesn't happen in Xterms, so
   it's no big deal, but...

2. When running X (so, part of the Xserver?) the screen NEVER turns off. So,
   unless I remember to put on a screensaver, the screen image just continues
   to burn into the monitor. If I remember to stop X before retiring for the
   night, the "regular" screen shuts itself off just fine (although it doesn't
   do the "deep sleep" - turn off power to the high voltage - like many PC's
   do today).

Thanks in advance for any suggestions.

-Bob Rinker
 



