> on the gnome-libs and the gtk.  Seems it doesn't like the
> alpha configuration. At the system type checks, I get
> 
> 'Invalid configuration 'alphapca56-unknown-linux-gnu':
> machine 'alphapca56-unknown' not recognized'
> 
> Any ideas how I can work around this?
> 
> Thanks,
> 
> Jason Colflesh

I had the same problem with lots of programs on the same alpha.

It it caused by the config.sub script file which doesn't recognies the
alphapca56 so when i have one of this problem, i edit every config.sub
in the directory tree and add two words at the begining of this file:

Look for a big bloc full of computer names separated with |
it looks like ... alphaxx | alphayy | alphazz \
and you just have to add the entry alphapca56

few lines later, you can find the same block with this time -* at the
end of each computer name you can do the same here
alphaxx-* | alphayy-* | alphazz-* \
and add alphapca56-*

I hope that in the nex version of the config.sub, they will add this
entry :)

bye



