I was having the same problems- RedHat 5.0, right?  Just got the answer this
afternoon (props to Jay Estabrook) on axp-list@redhat.com (great list BTW):

Get a new ramdisk.img from
ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/linux/redhat/redhat-5.0/updates/alpha/ramdisk.img
and make a new ramdisk floppy using
cd <the directory where you ftp'd it to>
dd if=ramdisk.img of=/dev/fd0 bs=1440k

With this new ramdisk, the installer should see the IDE drive.  (At least, it
did for me.)

An alternative: get RedHat 5.1, so you can install with the Redneck language!
:-)

