With 2.0.35, under the directory /usr/src/linux/drivers/net, there are two
files, tulip.c and tulip.c.axppatches.

I copied tulip.c to tulip.c.save (cp tulip.c tulip.c.save) and then copied
tulip.c.axppatches to tulip.c (cp tulip.c.axppatches tulip.c).

To be on the safe side, I also did this to ALL files under /usr/src/linux
subdirectories which had an additional axppatches file.  There were quite a
few.

Copied the /vmlinuz.gz file to /vmlinuz.gz.old to make sure if there was a
problem I could boot to the old kernel.

Then:

 make mrproper
 make config, Select Tulip under the PCI card options (Don�t select the DE
cards right before the Tulip card)
 make boot
 cp /usr/src/linux/arc/alpha/boot/vmlinuz.gz /

This worked for me.  I hope it helps you.

