> Bill Anderson@cyberhighway.net wrote:
>
> I have yet to get mine to respond at all. Would you mind letting you 
> know what steps you took to get it to work at all? I would *really*
> appreciate it.

First, I created a symbolic link from /dev/cua3 (DOS COM4) to /dev/modem.  I
started Minicom as root and configured the modem.  Here are my settings:

  Serial Device:          /dev/modem
  Bps/Par/Bits:           38400 8N1  
  Hardware Flow Control:  Yes
  Software Flow Control:  No
  Init string:            ~^M~AT S7=45 S0=1 L1 V1 X4 &c1 E1 Q0^M

I left the defaults for the rest of the settings.  

Once you get the modem working with Minicom, you can set up PPP with netcfg
(or some other tool, or hack the files by hand).  The default PPP setup
produced by netcfg works fine on my system.

Someone suggested running "setserial /dev/modem spd_hi" or "setserial
/dev/modem spd_hi" before dialing.  I did, and the modem quit hanging at the
higher speeds, but it will still only connect up to 31000.  I think that has
more to do with my phone lines and ISP than with my computer.

Richard Griswold




