"G. Hugh SONG" <ghsong@\"Spamspoiler\"kjist.ac.kr> writes:
> I installed the RedHat 5.1 on a fresh hard.
> Oh, no!   All the links and the directories are dated at year 2018.
> How can I fix this?  The month and day are all right.

I wrote a tiny program called "chyear":

syntax: ./chyear -(-a|-m) <filename> <from year> <to year>
  If access (-a) or modification (-m) time of <filename>
  falls in <from year>, it is changed to <to year>.


You can use it to do stuff like:

  foreach file ( `find . -mtime -0 -print` )
  chyear -m $file 2018 1998
  end


Source at:

  http://pauillac.inria.fr/~harley/tmp/chyear.c


Disclaimer: No warranty etc.

Bye,
  Rob.



