Organization: The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha,comp.lang.fortran

One way to get I have used to get around the problem with insertion of
record markers is to use access='direct' and a suitable record length
(recl=nnn).  This results in files without any record markers. The
downsize is that you have to write your records in the appropriate size
chunks and keep track of which record you are on (and specify it
in the write statement using irec=nn). Another problem as
far as portability is that with some fortran compilers  you specifiy
the record length in bytes, on others it is in 4 byte words. I can't
remember which g77 does.




