> One for the FAQ:
> ================
>
> The problem of XFree86 crashing when magnifying in xdvi or dragging
> icons in Netscape is due to some bad XFree86 rpms going around since
> June or so.
>
> To fix it get a new XF86_BLA, where BLA is something like SVGA.
> To find out do:
>
>   ls -l /usr/X11R6/bin/X*
>
> and you should see XF86_SVGA or something similar in the list.
>
> To get a fixed one you can download and install rpms from a RedHat
> updates directory.  The nearest one to me is:
>
>   ftp://ftp.lip6.fr/pub/linux/distributions/redhat/redhat-5.1/updates/alpha/
>
> (and you might as well update the rest of X while you're at it!).
> Alternatively, you could get a server patched by Matti Aarnio from:
>
>   ftp://mea.tmt.tele.fi/pub/XFree86/
>
> These alternatives work fine for RedHat 5.
>
> The "updated" X servers for RedHat 4 were still broken last time I
> checked.  So for RedHat 4 you should apply Matti's patches and compile
> your own, or you can fix the source yourself if you're courageous.
>
> The only reboots I have done for the last five or six months were:
>  1. Upgrade to 2.0.34
>  2. Upgrade to 2.0.35
>  3. Reboots when X crashed.
>
> My machine has been up since I fixed X.  I just put my fixed XF86_SVGA
> from XFree86 3.3.2, compiled on RedHat 4, at:
>
>   http://pauillac.inria.fr/~harley/tmp/Robs.XF86_SVGA.gz
>
> (1382980 bytes).  You ought to be using a recent XFree86 (i.e., 3.3.2)
> which runs Xwrapper which has permissions rws--x--x, and it runs X
> which should be a link to XF86_BLA.  If you aren't, upgrade to an
> updated XFree86 first.  Then as root:
>
>   cp Robs.XF86_SVGA.gz /usr/X11R6/bin/
>   cd /usr/X11R6/bin/
>   gunzip Robs.XF86_SVGA.gz
>   chmod 755 Robs.XF86_SVGA              /* No S-bits! */
>   rm X
>   ln -s Robs.XF86_SVGA X
>
> or something to that effect.
>
> Nota bene:
>   This works for me and I hope it does for you but I can't answer
>   technical questions about X (due to lack of knowledge, not lack of will).
>
> Bye,
>   Rob.



