"G. Hugh SONG" <ghsong@\"Spamspoiler\"kjist.ac.kr> wrote:

> I just heard that Dec FORTRAN (for alpha?) uses 4-byte record
> descriptor unlike g77 for alpha whcih uses 8-byte.  Is that really true?
> 
> If that is true, I can't understand g77's decision for 8-byte
> descriptor rather than 4-byte.
> 
> Can someone clarify this?

What I can clarify is that "decision" is the wrong word to use here - we 
detected the incompatibility (not being able to read unformatted files 
produced by a Dec Fortran compiled program in a g77 compiled one (on 
Alpha/DEC Unix) and vice versa) far too late to do anything on it.

Note (again - as I explained in a previous message) that the Fortran Standard 
doesn't guarantee you anything here, so this is just bad luck.

We're unlikely to "repair" this, as that would mean that files produced by 
g77-x.y.z would not be readable by g77-x.y.z+1, an even less preferable 
situation.

