  Here is what I use to write "real" binary files in the DEC-ALPHA
 to be transferred by FTP binary mode to DOS.

        integer*1 block(8000)

          open(17,file=fname,form='unformatted',recl=2000,
     1  recordtype='fixed',access='sequential',status='new')

         Write(17)block

There are no extra "record mark" (or whatever) bytes in the o/p.


I haven't found any way to go from DOS to ALPHA other than
by FTPing from DOS to ALPHA in binary mode and reading
512 bytes at a time into a circular store while stripping off the
(pre-known) "real"  record lengths. What a pain ! but after you
have written the subroutine - just feed it the "real" record length
and it's easy.

chris



