command:

boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
prompt_ramdisk=1"

you will need to have the boot floppy in the floppy drive to decompress the
vmlinux.gz image.  Then you will be asked to enter the ramdisk image.  Once the
ramdisk image installs, the setup screen will start asking the source for
installation, NFS, HD CD-ROM etc...

once you have installed the OS, you can reboot as follows:

boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags "root=/dev/yourscsi-or-ideHD" such as sda1,
sdb1, hda1 hda2 so on......

Good luck

