Both methods are very inefficient, because the chyear program has to be
started freshly for every file, resulting in high system cpu usage.
It's better to modify the program so it accepts any number of filenames
as arguments or reads them from stdin like the file I attached. This
way, the find results can be piped or backticked, resulting in only a
single call each of chyear and find.
I try to avoid -exec in find calls.

use
find . -mtime  -0 |chyear 2018 1998
or
chyear 2018 1998 `find . -mtime -0 -mount`

- Alex

