C. Ray Ng <crn1@cornell.edu> wrote:
: We are constantly writing large files over 2GB limit under 
: linux/alpha 2.0.32 and the earlier versions as well.
I had laboured under the impression that this was not possible.

: However, after upgraded to RH-5.1, files were truncated to
: 2^31 bytes long. This happened for both the official
: RH-5.1 CD as well as the powertool-5.1. 
It is definately the case that 2.0.35 limits file size to (2^31)-1 bytes. 
This is fixed in the 2.1 kernels.  The limit is imposed by the ext2 inode
format.  Please note that since inode layout changes between 2.0 and 2.1
