G. Hugh SONG wrote in message <6vunoh$loi$1@news.kjist.ac.kr>...

>The machine dependent constant setting routine called DMACH1 needs a
>selection of Double Precision format.  For DEC Alpha there are two
>choices; IEEE_format and G_float.  Which should I use for G77 on Linux?


I would be shocked if G77 wanted G_float on Alpha, because this is the
VAX-native floating point format, whereas IEEE-754 is the Alpha-native
format.  While current Alphas have some support for G_float numbers,
this support is rather limited.  So even knowing nothing about Linux
(note that its highest volume platform is the paradigm for IEEE-754)
or G77 (hasn't been ported to my platform), I would say that you almost
certainly want IEEE_format.  If you want to refute this point, please
don't do so in email because my email server is out of action for the
moment.





