James Van Buskirk wrote in message <6vurba$ac6@sjx-ixn3.ix.netcom.com>...
>I would be shocked if G77 wanted G_float on Alpha, because this is the
>VAX-native floating point format, whereas IEEE-754 is the Alpha-native
>format.  While current Alphas have some support for G_float numbers,
>this support is rather limited.

No, Alpha processor support for G_float is at an equal level to that for
IEEE (it's VAX D_float which is less supported), but at least for DIGITAL's
platforms, we support G_float on OpenVMS only.  I see no reason why
Linux/G77 couldn't support G_float on Alpha if it wanted to, but I suspect
that IEEE is the preferable choice there.

