> 
> Hrmm ...  I have a working install of redhat 5.1 from the srm, but would
> like to try the arc. If I do what you mention above, will it boot arc from
> ther out, and if so, can i switch back easily enough?
> 

Depends on the type of system you have.  Some can hold both the arc and
srm
firmware at the same time (I think the multia falls in the category). 
Typing
"arc" at the >>> prompt goes into the arc firmware and it will go there
every
time you boot.  To switch back to srm you use a menu selection and
somewhere
in there is an option to switch back to "Digital UNIX" or "Open VMS"
console.
On the next power cycle you will be back to srm.

Other systems (such as the AlphaStation 200) can only hold one firmware
image.
To switch between srm and arc you need to do a firmware update.  Check
out:

	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/

for firmware images.


- Doug



