I called QVS about this.  Part number

CC691P (IDC50P to SCSI II HPDB50F w/ Mounting Bracket)

This part has an IDC50 male end which allows the IDC50S (50-pin IDC cable
with female end) to plug directly in.  Apparently there is not a ribbon
cable with this, so it's more or less an adapter.  It costs $18, so I'm
going to buy it.  When I get it I'll post about it.

--Brian

PS - For those who didn't know (like me), the P in IDC50P means Pin (Male)
and IDC50S means Socket (Female).


