"Ric Stattin" <rstattin@parkcityus.com> writes:


> I have been looking around for info on how to get ecgs up and going on an
> DEC alpha lx running Red Hat 5.1 and have not had much luck.  Could someone
> please point in the right direction or give me the low down of the libraries
> and install-setup work?  I'm fairly new at Linux and programming, so at this
> point I'm pretty well lost.

5.1 comes with egcs-1.0.2 installed. If you want the latest and
greatest, you can either get rpms or you can download and untar the
sources, then

/configure --prefix=/usr/local/egcs-1.1b
make ; make install

then make symlinks like this:

ln -s /usr/local/egcs-1.1b/bin/gcc /usr/local/bin/gcc

etc. The compiler driver automatically looks at the path to determine
which libraries to use, so you can have multiple versions installed
this way and everything works fine.

-- g




