Subject: Sick multia (batteries)
Date: 1998/10/02
Message-ID: <6v36d9$pr2$1@Mars.mcs.net>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 397124132
Organization: MCSNet Services
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

My second Multia, which was sick (green screen, no boot) is well again.
Following is what happened. 

I put in 8MB known good RAM, got green screen (with or without system set
to failsafe boot from floppy).  Disconnected new battery, same thing.  
Left it without battery overnight, and it failsafe booted perfectly!  So
I ran the BLAST command toupdate flash to current SRM and ARC.  POwer
cycled, rebooted perfectly.

Now the fun.  Installed the battery, it would not boot (green screen).
Remove the battery, green screen.  Wait a while, and it boots again.
Checked my new noname relacement battery and its putting out 5.8 volts
(its supposed to be 4.5 volts).  I mickeymoused 3 AA batteries in a 
holder with the correct plug.  Multia boots perfectly, with or without
this battery pack installed.

So it looks like there's an additional failure mode, worth noting since
I recall seeing apost or two about someone installing a 6v battery in
their Multia... overvoltage can also cause screwy problems.  The battery
pack I have now is putting out 4.65 and I've had no more problems.  I'm
going to locate  a brand-name replacement (so it'll fit inside) and 
make certain to doublecheck the voltage prior to install...

Rich Jordan
rjordan@mcs.net




